  "result": "Perfect! All 240 tests pass. I've successfully implemented the customer statements feature:\n\n**Created src/statements.js:**\n- `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` \u2014 generates a customer statement:\n  - Validates customer exists (CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND error if not)\n  - Normalizes customer ID\n  - Filters invoices to only include:\n    - Invoices for the specified customer\n    - Status 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (excludes 'draft' and 'paid')\n    - issueDate on or before asOf date\n  - Maps each invoice to: { number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }\n    - due is calculated using balanceDue from payments module\n  - Sorts invoices by issueDate ascending\n  - Calculates totalDue (sum of all due amounts)\n  - Returns ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })\n\n**Comprehensive test coverage (240 tests total; 17 new):**\n- Empty statements for customers with no invoices\n- Customer validation and error handling\n- Date filtering (on/before asOf date)\n- Invoice status filtering (issued, partially_paid only)\n- Customer ID normalization with spaces and mixed case\n- Correct calculation of due amounts (including partial payments)\n- Sorting by issueDate\n- Multiple customers in same invoice array\n- Interaction with vouchers and discounts\n- Edge cases (asOf date exactly matching issueDate)\n\nAll house rules followed: no argument mutation, Result pattern for errors, customer ID normalization, all tests passing.",
